# ESP32: Wi-Fi and a relay
# Level 5 - Advanced
#
# The same language on an ESP32: its pin names, a pull-down button, a relay, and a Wi-Fi status light.
# You learn: changing the board line, GPIO pin names, secret() for passwords and wifi.connected.
# You need: an ESP32 DevKit, an LED on GPIO26, a button from GPIO27 to 3.3V, and a relay module on GPIO25.
# Add your Wi-Fi as a secret called home_wifi first (Project > Secrets) - passwords never go in the code.

board esp32

status = pin GPIO26 as output
button = pin GPIO27 as input pulldown   # pressed = 3.3 V
relay  = pin GPIO25 as output inverted

var relay_on = false

at start:
    wifi.connect(secret("home_wifi"))   # connects in the background and reconnects by itself

every 1 s:
    status.write(wifi.connected)        # the LED shows the Wi-Fi link

on button.pressed:
    relay_on = not relay_on
    relay.write(relay_on)
    log.info "Relay {relay_on}"

every 1 min:
    log.info "Up {board.uptime}, free memory {board.free_memory}, Wi-Fi {wifi.connected}"
